NOT COVERED BY THE ABOVE
========================

uniwill-laptop/
    GPL-2.0-or-later. Derived from tuxedo-drivers (TUXEDO Computers GmbH),
    which is GPL-2.0-or-later, so it cannot be relicensed. Its own LICENSE
    file governs. This is a one-way boundary: MIT code may be used inside a
    GPL work, but GPL code may not be moved out into the MIT part of this
    tree. Do not copy code from uniwill-laptop/ into hydroc/ or kbctrl/.

Runtime dependencies are installed separately by the user and are not
distributed with this software:

    ite8291r3-ctl   GPL-2.0   keyboard RGB transport, imported by kbctrl
    acpi_call       GPL-2.0   kernel module, how the daemon reaches the EC

Hardware protocol details in this tree were reverse-engineered, or read from
published drivers and reimplemented. Register addresses, packet layouts and
bit assignments are facts about the hardware and carry no licence. Sources
consulted are credited in DESIGN.md.
